<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n62347" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λεκτικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>good at speaking, able to speak</i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				4.3.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				5.5.46
			</span></i> (
				Sup.
			); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ -κή</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέχνη</span>) <i>the art of speaking</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Plt.</u>
				304d
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>suited for speaking</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ λ. τῶν
				λόγων</span> speeches <i>in common colloquial style</i>,
			opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποιητικῶς συγκείμενοι</span>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				61.2
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάλιστα λ. τῶν μέτρων τὸ ἰαμβεῖόν
					ἐστι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Po.</u>
					1449a24
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1408b33
			</span></i>. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῶς</span>
			<i>in prose</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Comp.</u>
				25
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>related to expression, stylistic</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ
				λ. τόπος</span> the province <i>of expression</i>,
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				4
			</span></i>; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πραγματικός</span>, <i>of
				style</i>, opp. matter, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρεταί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Pomp.</u>
					1
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Th.</u>
					34
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῶς</span>
			<i>with the force of a word</i>, of the termination -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεν</span>, <i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Adv.</u>
				195.16
			</span></i>; <i>verbally,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Stoic.
				3.214
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
